{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:encoder:)","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:transport:encoder:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/Destination-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPTransport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One request per batch, in the order the delivery hands them over, the next sent only once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the previous one has a response or has failed."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The method is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST"},{"type":"text","text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the batch’s first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record, then "},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names are the instrument’s: ","type":"text"},{"code":"traceparent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracestate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NoOpInstrument","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a batch may hold"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the body, where a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" writes it."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType"},{"text":", whatever a configured","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field or the instrument wrote.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the batch’s records, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived. Any other status, or no response,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"means it didn’t; either way the batch is not sent again.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record can still arrive twice: one a store redelivers after the app was stopped mid-send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") may have arrived before. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the one it was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first sent with, so an encoder that writes each record’s identifier lets the server keep one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copy.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" handles its own failures: a batch the encoder can’t encode, a send that gets","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no response and a response that isn’t 2xx are each logged at error level and dropped, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the delivery and its other destinations carry on. A cancelled delivery cancels the send in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flight, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" returns without logging it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","tex